1.  MISSION CONFIRMS TRADE ADVISOR THOMAS GEWECKE
WILL ATTEND SUBJECT CONFERENCE.
2.  IN ADDITION TO ITEMS PROPOSED IN BRUSSELS 15642,
WE SUGGEST AGENDA COULD ADDRESS:
(A)  SECTORAL TRADE PROBLEMS SUCH AS STEEL;
(B)  COMPETITION FROM NEWLY INDUSTRIALIZING
COUNTRIES;
(C)  POSITIVE ADJUSTMENT POLICIES;
(D)  PROBLEMS OF EXPORT CREDIT COMPETITION.
RYAN

UNSSOD PREPCOM V
PASS TO ACDA/PERSONNEL
1.  FOR PERIOD APRIL 4 THRU APRIL 22, 1978:
JULIA B. KRENZEL:  4/4 - 1-OT; 4/5 - 1-OT; 4/6 - 2-OT;
4/7 - 1-OT; 4/8 - 3-OT; 4/10 - 2-OT; 4/11 - 2.5-OT;
4/12 - 2-OT; 4/13 - 8-SL; 4/14 - 8-SL; 4/17 - 1-OT;
4/18 - 2-OT; 4/19 - 3-OT; 4/20 - 2-OT; 4/21 - 2-OT;
4/22 - 5-OT.  YOUNG

1.  VISAS:  ONE WESTERN HEMISPHERE; ONE AUSTRALIA SECOND 72;
ONE BELGIUM NP 37; ONE CYPRUS FIFTH 202; ONE CZECHOSLOVAKIA NP 38;
ONE EGYPT FIFTH 327; ONE FRANCE THIRD 108; SIX FRANCE NP 111 THRU
116; ONE MONTSERRAT SECOND 44; THREE GREECE FIFTH 1692 THRU 1694;
THREE HUNGARY SECOND 69 THRU 71; ONE PHILIPPINES SECOND 3296; ONE
PHILIPPINES THIRD 3297; ONE USSR NP 87.
HARPER

